##### 1.2 Static Callback Overwrite in iOS Gemma Installer
- **Location**: [`GemmaBaseModelInstaller.ios.kt:22-58`](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PayslipMAX%20KMP/shared/src/iosMain/kotlin/com/payslipmax/pdfparser/insights/gemma/GemmaBaseModelInstaller.ios.kt#L22-L58)
- **Why it is High Severity**:
  `progressReporter` and `completionReporter` are stored as static `var`s on the `companion object`. When [`PayslipViewModel`](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PayslipMAX%20KMP/composeApp/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/payslipmax/pdfparser/ui/PayslipViewModel.kt) (registered as a `factory` in Koin) is resolved again or re-created during lifecycle changes, the newly instantiated installer overwrites the global static listeners with closures pointing to its own `_state`. Any previously active screen/subscriber gets orphaned and stops receiving download updates.
- **Chance of Regression**: **Low – Medium (15–25%)**
  - **Remediation**: Make `IosGemmaBaseModelInstaller` a Koin `single` (singleton) rather than re-creating it per ViewModel, or migrate static callback vars to a multi-listener flow / listener registry.
  - **Regression Vectors**: 
    1. Changing callback lifecycles could cause strong reference cycles / memory leaks between Swift's `NSBundleResourceRequest` and the Kotlin runtime.
    2. Modifying the `companion object` interface impacts [`GemmaOnDemandResourceBridge.swift`](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PayslipMAX%20KMP/iosApp/iosApp/GemmaOnDemandResourceBridge.swift), requiring careful synchronized verification on iOS.

