#### 2. Medium Severity

##### 2.1 `FLAG_SECURE` Disabled for Foreground App
- **Location**: [`MainActivity.kt:20-38`](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PayslipMAX%20KMP/composeApp/src/androidMain/kotlin/com/payslipmax/pdfparser/MainActivity.kt#L20-L38)
- **Why it is Medium Severity**:
  [`shouldApplyFlagSecure(isDebug)`](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PayslipMAX%20KMP/composeApp/src/androidMain/kotlin/com/payslipmax/pdfparser/MainActivity.kt#L23) returns `false` unconditionally. While the background app switcher is protected (`setRecentsScreenshotEnabled(false)` on Android 13+), the foreground app does not block screenshots, screen recording, or mirroring of sensitive defense salary/PAN data.
- **Chance of Regression**: **Medium (35–45% User Experience / Functional Impact)**
  - **Remediation**: Returning `!isDebug` enables `FLAG_SECURE` for store release builds.
  - **Regression Vectors**:
    1. **User frustration**: Armed forces personnel frequently take screenshots of their tax/allowance breakdowns or calculation cards to share with accountants or banks; `FLAG_SECURE` renders all captured screenshots completely black.
    2. **Support impact**: Users cannot capture screenshots of errors or edge-case slips when submitting feedback/bug reports.
    3. **Automated testing / Accessibility**: Screen-recording tools, UI automation, and certain accessibility tools fail on secured windows.

##### 2.2 Room Database Destructive Migration Fallback
- **Location**: [`PayslipDatabase.android.kt:15`](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PayslipMAX%20KMP/shared/src/androidMain/kotlin/com/payslipmax/pdfparser/database/PayslipDatabase.kt#L15), [`PayslipDatabase.ios.kt:16`](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PayslipMAX%20KMP/shared/src/iosMain/kotlin/com/payslipmax/pdfparser/database/PayslipDatabase.kt#L16)
- **Why it is Medium Severity**:
  Both database builders enable `.fallbackToDestructiveMigration(true)`. If a future developer modifies an entity or schema version without providing an explicit or auto-migration path, Room will silently drop and recreate all user database tables, permanently erasing user payslips and ledger history.
- **Chance of Regression**: **Medium (30% Operational Risk)**
  - **Remediation**: Disable destructive migration fallback for release builds and enforce strict migration tests.
  - **Regression Vectors**:
    If `.fallbackToDestructiveMigration(false)` is applied before all migration paths are exhaustively verified with `MigrationTestHelper`, any missed schema change will cause an unrecoverable `IllegalStateException` crash on cold launch for updating users.

##### 2.3 `x86_64` Simulator Incompatibility on iOS
- **Location**: [`iosApp.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj`](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PayslipMAX%20KMP/iosApp/iosApp.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj), [`LiteRTLM.xcframework`](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PayslipMAX%20KMP/iosApp/Vendor/LiteRTLM)
- **Why it is Medium Severity**:
  `CLiteRTLM.xcframework` contains only `arm64` binaries. Building for generic iOS Simulators or on Intel Macs fails linking because `x86_64` is not excluded under `EXCLUDED_ARCHS`.
- **Chance of Regression**: **Negligible (< 2%)**
  - **Remediation**: Add `x86_64` to `EXCLUDED_ARCHS[sdk=iphonesimulator*]` in the Xcode project.
  - **Why Regression is Low**: Builds on Intel Macs already fail today. Excluding `x86_64` prevents the linker error and has zero impact on physical devices or Apple Silicon (`arm64`) simulators.

##### 2.4 Incomplete Public `initKoin()`
- **Location**: [`Koin.kt:72-75`](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PayslipMAX%20KMP/shared/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/payslipmax/pdfparser/di/Koin.kt#L72-L75)
